  "title": "IMABS computes CRT hypot(re, im) without squaring underflow and rejects empty text with #NUM!",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20430 and 20527, IMABS(inumber) parses complex text to 15 significant digits (rejecting empty text \"\" with #NUM! while treating a blank cell as 0) and computes modulus via CRT hypot(re, im), preserving tiny values such as 1e-300 without the squaring underflow seen in IMSQRT. All 1,209 full-bank IMABS rows match.",
